[?2004lpages: 1
--- page 1 ---
Mixbench Monthly, issue 87, April 2026 — Tarnwell Micaform 1.0 reviewed
Reviewed by Ines Calloway. Excerpt kept for the studio's own evaluation.
Owners of Tarnwell's TM-9 modelling microphone have until now reached its capsule models
through the Racklane host: a Capsule module feeding a Valve Stage module, one lane per
microphone. Micaform folds that chain into a single plugin.
The front panel puts Proximity and Intensity within easy reach. Neither is new: the earlier Racklane
Capsule module had both controls, tucked away on its second page. Here they sit where your hand
already is.
A valve drive stage follows the capsule, and a tape stage follows that, so the whole chain lives in
one window. The tape stage here runs clean: there is no wow control on it, and nothing to make it
wobble.
The dual capsule blend is the real news. Micaform blends two capsule models inside one instance,
something the Racklane chain could only do across two lanes.
There are omissions. Version 1.0 offers no oversampling option, and there is no sidechain input, so
anyone who keyed the Racklane Valve Stage from a kick drum will have to find another route.
A word on the old setup too: the earlier Racklane chain had no low cut of its own, and you reached
for a separate EQ.
Verdict: an easy recommendation for TM-9 owners who never went looking in the rack's more
obscure corners.

